1. THE LAW: A ∪ B = B ∪ A, A ∩ B = B ∩ A; (A ∪ B) ∪ C = A ∪ (B ∪ C), (A ∩ B) ∩ C = A ∩ (B ∩ C)
   checked on all 4096 choices of 3 subset(s) of U = {1, 2, 3, 4}: True

2. ONE INSTANCE, WORKED
   A = {1, 2}, B = {2, 3}, C = {3, 4}, A' = {3, 4}, B' = {1, 4}
   A ∪ B = {1, 2, 3} = B ∪ A = {1, 2, 3}
   (A ∪ B) ∪ C = {1, 2, 3, 4} = A ∪ (B ∪ C) = {1, 2, 3, 4}

3. THE SAME LAW IN LOGIC: p ∨ q = q ∨ p, (p ∨ q) ∨ r = p ∨ (q ∨ r), and the same for ∧
   every row of the truth table agrees, which is why the member-by-member check is a proof:
   p  q  r   left  right
   T  T  T   T     T
   T  T  F   T     T
   T  F  T   T     T
   T  F  F   T     T
   F  T  T   T     T
   F  T  F   T     T
   F  F  T   T     T
   F  F  F   F     F
